WEBVTT

00:11.480 --> 00:14.300
<i>I have to make it through 
the evening party without</i>

00:14.300 --> 00:16.620
<i>Count Lawvine discovering my double identity.</i>

00:17.240 --> 00:18.370
<i>And...</i>

00:19.060 --> 00:22.750
<i>I'd like to somehow find a way to get 
Prince Kyle to take this medicine.</i>

00:22.750 --> 00:25.380
<i>If he doesn't receive treatment, 
in the near future...</i>

00:25.380 --> 00:28.720
<i>his illness will keep him
from even being able to stand.</i>

00:38.180 --> 00:39.660
What a surprise.

00:41.580 --> 00:44.270
I thought that anyone caring for 
an herb garden of this sort...

00:44.270 --> 00:48.450
must be someone in a profession 
similar to mine, but...

00:50.680 --> 00:52.010
Good evening,

00:52.960 --> 00:55.270
person who seems to be akin to me.

00:58.610 --> 01:00.180
<i>Professor Michel!</i>

02:49.020 --> 02:50.780
What do you think of the aurora?

02:51.430 --> 02:53.410
Has it given you a hint to your research?

02:53.410 --> 02:55.520
Yes! Very much so!

02:55.520 --> 02:57.280
I'm glad to hear that.

02:57.280 --> 03:01.580
I'm sorry, Professor, asking you to 
travel all this way to bring me here.

03:01.580 --> 03:03.290
Why are you apologizing?

03:03.820 --> 03:06.290
You're my student,

03:06.800 --> 03:10.290
so whatever it is you want to 
see, I want to help you see it.

03:10.670 --> 03:13.240
If there's something you 
don't know, I'll teach you.

03:13.800 --> 03:17.690
Though, when you want to achieve something 
solely through your own efforts, I won't interfere.

03:22.220 --> 03:26.430
<i>In my third life, this man was my teacher.</i>

03:28.330 --> 03:31.990
Pardon my insolence, but may I ask your name?

03:33.380 --> 03:36.570
Oh, my apologies if I've startled you.

03:37.010 --> 03:38.750
I am Michel Hévin.

03:39.290 --> 03:41.110
I'm here from Coyolles.

03:41.880 --> 03:43.660
If you've lost your way,

03:43.660 --> 03:45.620
we can escort you back to your room.

03:45.620 --> 03:47.380
How kind of you.

03:47.380 --> 03:49.290
But I'm not lost.

03:49.820 --> 03:52.140
I'm interested in the young lady there.

03:52.780 --> 03:54.030
This individual is our empire's—

03:54.030 --> 03:55.360
It's all right.

03:58.920 --> 04:01.550
My name is Rishe Irmgard Weitzner.

04:02.250 --> 04:04.740
Master Hévin, might you be a scholar?

04:04.740 --> 04:06.470
A scholar, you say?

04:06.470 --> 04:09.220
That may be the simplest way to put it.

04:10.880 --> 04:12.230
Your nails.

04:12.560 --> 04:14.600
You used sap from the 
gelwood tree, didn't you?

04:15.100 --> 04:17.480
Though, it seems you've 
used dyes to add color.

04:18.980 --> 04:22.080
What method did you use to harden it?

04:22.080 --> 04:25.880
I took lish grass and gibi 
nectar, added labed leaf,

04:25.880 --> 04:27.990
and compounded them together with glue.

04:27.990 --> 04:31.620
Did you refrain from using kirith 
leaf in order to prevent air bubbles?

04:31.620 --> 04:34.000
You seem to know everything about it already.

04:34.330 --> 04:36.870
It's no more than a logic-based theory.

04:38.120 --> 04:41.010
What do you think would happen 
if you mixed in some estoma sap?

04:42.980 --> 04:45.340
I think it might harden even further.

04:45.840 --> 04:48.350
Though, that's only a hypothesis, at most.

04:48.350 --> 04:51.270
The actual results would 
require verification.

04:51.530 --> 04:53.720
You're quite an admirable young lady.

04:53.720 --> 04:57.270
So admirable that were it possible, I 
would like to take you as my apprentice.

04:59.300 --> 05:02.200
If you wouldn't mind, just for the 
time that you're staying here,

05:02.200 --> 05:04.570
may I receive your 
instruction on various matters?

05:04.570 --> 05:06.820
Yes. I don't mind at all.

05:07.070 --> 05:08.780
Thank you so much!

05:08.780 --> 05:12.040
Then, Master Hévin, this means 
you'll be like a professor to me!

05:12.040 --> 05:13.600
A professor, is it?

05:14.580 --> 05:16.400
That sounds like fun.

05:18.400 --> 05:23.420
<i>I never imagined the day would come that 
I'd be able to call him "Professor" again.</i>

05:27.990 --> 05:29.860
By the way, my student,

05:30.760 --> 05:35.540
the herbs in this garden lie 
slightly outside my expertise,

05:35.540 --> 05:37.440
so this is only a guess,

05:39.260 --> 05:43.190
but are you perhaps intending 
to give Kyle some manner of medicine?

05:48.450 --> 05:53.450
Lady Rishe, I never imagined I'd have the 
good fortune of seeing you twice in one day.

05:53.730 --> 05:57.330
Please, don't hold to formalities 
for my sake. Speak as you wish.

05:57.330 --> 05:59.950
Then, if I may take you at your word...

06:01.460 --> 06:04.920
Michel, what are you doing?

06:04.920 --> 06:07.180
I've found this amazing girl!

06:07.180 --> 06:09.140
I thought you might want 
to meet her, too, Kyle.

06:09.140 --> 06:12.790
This individual is His Highness, 
the crown prince's fiancée.

06:12.790 --> 06:14.800
Really? Is she?

06:15.250 --> 06:18.400
But she's become my student, you see?

06:18.400 --> 06:19.230
What?

06:20.580 --> 06:24.360
The herbal medicine she's compounded 
seems like it would work for you, Kyle.

06:24.360 --> 06:25.650
Herbal medicine?

06:26.120 --> 06:31.370
It's outside my field, but I felt you 
should be used in this experiment, Kyle.

06:31.370 --> 06:35.740
Professor! You shouldn't use the 
prince of a kingdom in an experiment!

06:35.740 --> 06:38.680
Oh, have I made a blunder?

06:38.680 --> 06:41.330
Common sense is such a 
difficult thing, isn't it?

06:41.330 --> 06:46.050
But I truly do, from the bottom of 
my heart, want Kyle to get well.

06:47.600 --> 06:48.580
All right.

06:48.580 --> 06:50.260
Are you sure?

06:50.720 --> 06:54.700
The greatest scholar in my kingdom 
says he wants me to try this medicine.

06:54.700 --> 06:55.760
From the beginning...

06:56.140 --> 07:01.150
I have been resolved to use any method 
necessary to cure this disease.

07:03.100 --> 07:05.980
Then, I will prepare it immediately.

07:11.660 --> 07:12.940
Here it is.

07:14.720 --> 07:18.440
The truth is that there is one 
problem with this medicine.

07:19.520 --> 07:20.860
Please, tell us.

07:22.790 --> 07:24.380
This medicine...

07:26.530 --> 07:28.670
is incredibly revolting in flavor.

07:29.130 --> 07:30.900
The flavor is incredibly revolting?

07:32.280 --> 07:34.530
Oh, is that all?

07:34.530 --> 07:36.460
Kyle will be just fine.

07:36.460 --> 07:38.950
After all, he's a very strong boy.

07:38.950 --> 07:40.800
He's earnest and hard-working, too.

07:40.800 --> 07:41.560
Right?

07:42.640 --> 07:47.490
Lady Rishe, if this is the ordeal 
which has been bestowed upon me,

07:47.490 --> 07:50.190
I need only face it down with 
all of my strength and spirit.

07:51.700 --> 07:54.070
I know. I'll feed it to you!

07:54.950 --> 07:57.950
Professor! You mustn't! At 
least ready some water first!

07:56.200 --> 07:57.120
Here you go.

07:57.120 --> 07:57.950
Wait, I—

08:04.150 --> 08:06.040
Are you all right?

08:08.490 --> 08:09.910
I am.

08:10.710 --> 08:12.840
So, Kyle, what does it taste like?

08:12.840 --> 08:14.230
What is the flavor like?

08:15.590 --> 08:18.350
Bitter mixed with sour, and 
mingled with the two...

08:18.350 --> 08:22.300
a particular stench, like that 
of a horse stable, swoops in.

08:22.300 --> 08:27.360
Th-Then, after swallowing, a strange 
sweetness wraps around the tongue like a slimy—

08:27.360 --> 08:29.660
There's no need to explain each stage!

08:29.660 --> 08:31.680
Shall we try to get a clearer 
grasp of the flavor?

08:29.660 --> 08:32.110
Excuse me! Please bring some water!

08:31.680 --> 08:32.110
Y-Yes, sir!

08:32.750 --> 08:34.140
Here. One more sip.

08:34.140 --> 08:35.370
Professor!

08:42.800 --> 08:47.660
Now, my student, would you like to look 
at this until your escort arrives?

08:55.300 --> 08:56.840
Professor, this is—!

08:56.840 --> 08:59.110
My research records.

08:59.570 --> 09:01.280
They're too difficult for Kyle.

09:01.280 --> 09:04.230
He said that no one would 
be able to understand them.

09:08.760 --> 09:11.490
You truly are a most intriguing girl.

09:18.670 --> 09:22.460
<i>Rishe, you truly hate 
this medicine, don't you?</i>

09:27.400 --> 09:29.240
You're an intelligent girl.

09:29.240 --> 09:31.090
If you have a flaw,

09:31.630 --> 09:37.520
it might be that you only want to use your 
knowledge and skills to make people happy.

09:38.320 --> 09:43.090
I think it's a mistake for you 
to determine others' happiness.

09:44.560 --> 09:47.520
If something is born into this world 
as a poison, then its reason for being...

09:47.520 --> 09:51.520
would be to fulfill its role and bring 
misfortune to people, don't you think?

09:52.850 --> 09:57.650
Is it truly impossible for a poison 
to bring someone happiness?

09:59.320 --> 10:02.080
The idea that someone is born 
to bring misfortune to others...

10:02.080 --> 10:05.160
that preconception in itself 
isn't like you, Professor.

10:05.840 --> 10:07.820
There's no need to worry.

10:07.820 --> 10:09.920
This compound hasn't been perfected yet.

10:11.010 --> 10:15.860
It's complete, but I've been unable to obtain
 the human resources necessary for testing.

10:15.860 --> 10:19.430
Someone who will use this 
compound exactly as I wish...

10:19.760 --> 10:21.760
Such a person doesn't exist.

10:24.380 --> 10:26.120
<i>The professor and I...</i>

10:27.120 --> 10:30.790
<i>we just couldn't come to understand each 
other when it came to that compound.</i>

10:31.480 --> 10:35.720
<i>I wonder if the professor has met the 
kind of person he was looking for.</i>

10:37.950 --> 10:39.860
P-Pardon the intrusion!

10:40.340 --> 10:42.230
Lady Rishe, your escort has arrived.

10:43.370 --> 10:44.210
What?

10:44.860 --> 10:46.660
Rishe, we're leaving.

10:46.660 --> 10:48.370
Prince Arnold...

10:48.660 --> 10:50.520
Your Highness, why are you here?

10:57.660 --> 11:00.030
This is Michel Hévin, a scholar.

11:00.030 --> 11:01.770
He is incredibly knowledgeable

11:01.770 --> 11:05.180
and he'll be teaching me all 
sorts of things while he's here.

11:06.610 --> 11:09.120
I am honored to receive such an introduction.

11:09.120 --> 11:12.840
I suppose I should present 
myself as well as possible here.

11:14.570 --> 11:15.850
Good evening.

11:15.850 --> 11:18.480
You're this empire's crown prince, I assume?

11:19.360 --> 11:23.440
It seems you've granted permission for 
us to enter your imperial library.

11:23.440 --> 11:25.160
Thank you.

11:25.160 --> 11:29.450
If you should require anything for your 
exchange of knowledge with my future wife,

11:29.450 --> 11:31.160
I will procure it.

11:31.160 --> 11:32.650
Ask for whatever it may be.

11:34.740 --> 11:38.160
Then, I won't refrain from 
making many requests of you.

11:40.590 --> 11:42.800
Why did you suddenly come to escort me?

11:42.800 --> 11:44.300
I was on my way back anyway.

11:44.740 --> 11:47.570
Are you always out and about this late?

11:47.570 --> 11:49.680
When I become absorbed in my work,

11:49.680 --> 11:51.740
I find myself forgetting the time.

11:52.460 --> 11:56.110
Oh, but I slept until this afternoon, 
so please don't worry.

11:58.960 --> 11:59.570
Here.

12:05.320 --> 12:06.720
Use that.

12:06.720 --> 12:10.000
What? But this pocket watch 
is such a precious item!

12:10.000 --> 12:13.630
It doesn't bother me. Since 
it's easy to carry around,

12:13.630 --> 12:15.710
I found it convenient to have for battles.

12:15.710 --> 12:19.590
By "battles," do you mean 
in strategizing for battles?

12:19.590 --> 12:24.080
Yes. There are some who doubt them 
because they haven't existed for long,

12:24.080 --> 12:26.600
but it's just a tool which 
accurately tells the time.

12:27.500 --> 12:31.020
<i>His Highness's thinking is flexible 
enough to adopt new technologies.</i>

12:32.780 --> 12:36.270
Someone who will use this 
compound exactly as I wish...

12:36.850 --> 12:38.830
Such a person doesn't exist.

12:43.630 --> 12:44.700
What is it?

12:44.700 --> 12:46.000
It's nothing.

12:46.430 --> 12:49.970
I'll take you at your word and 
indulge myself by borrowing this.

12:49.970 --> 12:55.080
Now that I think about it, my master 
in herbalism found these useful, too.

12:55.080 --> 12:56.640
Your master?

12:56.640 --> 13:01.090
Yes. A truly incredible 
herbalist from Renhua.

13:01.410 --> 13:04.530
How does that man compare 
to this master of yours?

13:04.530 --> 13:07.840
Professor Michel isn't an herbalist.

13:07.840 --> 13:11.580
Though, he does use herbal medicines in 
his research, so he has the knowledge.

13:11.580 --> 13:13.850
Then who is he?

13:14.230 --> 13:19.410
He researches all the substances in 
 the world and creates new substances.

13:19.410 --> 13:21.230
That's the sort of scholar he is.

13:21.230 --> 13:24.110
He creates new substances, you say?

13:24.110 --> 13:29.370
In Professor Michel's case, he says that 
his objective isn't the creation of gold,

13:29.370 --> 13:33.470
but if we were to call him by the title 
which most closely describes his work...

13:35.690 --> 13:38.150
it would be "alchemist."

13:47.020 --> 13:48.710
<i>At tonight's party,</i>

13:48.710 --> 13:53.630
<i>I have to act cleverly so that Count 
Lawvine doesn't notice anything.</i>

13:55.620 --> 13:56.520
Lady Rishe.

13:56.930 --> 13:58.710
A letter has arrived for you.

13:58.710 --> 13:59.650
Thank you.

14:02.650 --> 14:04.360
<i>Madame Mihaela.</i>

14:08.340 --> 14:11.530
<i>I said that the piece would 
take a month to complete,</i>

14:11.530 --> 14:15.570
<i>but I've made a request of an artisan 
visiting Galkhein from Coyolles,</i>

14:15.570 --> 14:18.830
<i>so it's likely that the date of 
delivery will be much sooner.</i>

14:18.830 --> 14:22.680
<i>Changing artisans makes 
this much of a difference?</i>

14:28.470 --> 14:29.870
How beautiful!

14:51.370 --> 14:52.450
Your Highness.

14:52.450 --> 14:55.920
The fact that you find
this tedious is showing.

14:55.920 --> 14:57.200
I'm showing that on purpose.

14:57.460 --> 14:58.450
It isn't a problem.

14:59.660 --> 15:00.900
Prince Arnold.

15:02.880 --> 15:06.030
For you to prepare an event 
such as this for my sake...

15:06.030 --> 15:07.700
I am entirely unworthy of it.

15:08.180 --> 15:12.090
Lady Rishe, tonight you are 
indescribably beautiful.

15:12.390 --> 15:13.910
Thank you.

15:14.320 --> 15:16.850
How do you find you've 
been feeling since then?

15:17.210 --> 15:19.980
Thanks to you, I'm feeling much better.

15:19.980 --> 15:21.690
That's the most important thing.

15:22.440 --> 15:26.860
Prince Arnold, I'm going to 
go and speak with the ladies.

15:27.190 --> 15:30.300
Prince Kyle, please do enjoy yourself.

15:36.280 --> 15:38.060
<i>I've finished giving my greetings,</i>

15:38.060 --> 15:40.640
<i>so I've met my most basic obligations.</i>

15:41.520 --> 15:42.870
<i>All that's left is...</i>

15:46.750 --> 15:49.520
<i>Now... focus.</i>

16:17.870 --> 16:19.030
<i>I found him.</i>

16:19.660 --> 16:22.890
<i>It's been a while, but that went very well.</i>

16:22.890 --> 16:27.230
<i>I never imagined that experience from my fifth 
life would prove useful in a place like this.</i>

16:34.680 --> 16:37.190
<i>I must keep my focus...</i>

16:38.180 --> 16:42.890
<i>and keep anyone from noticing 
that I'm avoiding Count Lawvine.</i>

16:40.680 --> 16:42.890
How are you, Lady Rishe?

16:43.490 --> 16:44.630
How are you?

16:45.490 --> 16:48.310
I'm honored to meet you, Lady Rishe.

16:48.310 --> 16:53.680
No, the honor is mine. I'm very happy 
to speak with you, Lord Weilman.

16:54.160 --> 16:58.580
After hearing what happened from my mother, 
I've been looking forward to meeting you.

16:58.580 --> 17:01.200
Your mother?

17:01.200 --> 17:05.460
I heard that you were kind enough to 
visit my mother's shop the other day.

17:05.460 --> 17:07.800
He can't mean that that 
difficult proprietress...

17:07.800 --> 17:10.710
Even Her Majesty, the empress 
wasn't accepted as a client.

17:10.960 --> 17:13.340
Oh, could you mean...

17:13.780 --> 17:18.470
I'm the proprietor of this 
store, Mihaela Laure Weilman.

17:19.740 --> 17:21.850
I merely picked out a stone.

17:21.850 --> 17:24.890
The one who sought to purchase 
something there was Prince Arnold.

17:24.890 --> 17:25.900
My!

17:25.900 --> 17:28.520
Prince Arnold giving a woman jewelry?

17:28.520 --> 17:30.830
<i>I was surprised, too.</i>

17:31.880 --> 17:36.820
Speaking of which, I was informed that the 
delivery date will be much sooner than anticipated.

17:36.820 --> 17:41.260
I understand that it's because an artisan 
from Coyolles was entrusted with the work,

17:41.260 --> 17:43.410
but would that really make 
this great a difference?

17:43.710 --> 17:48.300
Coyolles' jewelry artisans 
possess superior techniques.

17:48.300 --> 17:51.340
The speed they can complete fine, 
detailed work at is completely different.

17:51.600 --> 17:56.260
Really? I suppose I should expect no less 
from a country which produces gems and metals.

17:58.800 --> 18:01.490
<i>Count Lawvine seems to be standing still.</i>

18:09.720 --> 18:11.230
Prince Arnold,

18:11.230 --> 18:15.400
please, will you lend Coyolles your strength?

18:16.160 --> 18:18.850
Instead of aid through money or medical care,

18:18.850 --> 18:22.170
we would like to receive Galkhein's 
support through military means.

18:23.850 --> 18:27.600
As you know, Coyolles' military 
strength is all but nonexistent.

18:28.250 --> 18:34.080
Our kingdom is allowed to exist 
because we provide gems and metals.

18:35.170 --> 18:38.160
If our neighboring nations so wished,

18:38.160 --> 18:40.510
they could destroy us at any 
time, and they threaten to do so.

18:41.670 --> 18:43.890
I want to extricate us from this situation

18:43.890 --> 18:46.380
and obtain a method to protect our citizens!

18:48.000 --> 18:52.520
You're saying that Coyolles wants 
to forge an alliance with Galkhein.

18:52.520 --> 18:54.070
It's just as you say.

18:57.290 --> 19:00.050
I've been wondering what 
you were going to say.

19:00.050 --> 19:05.290
You pushed your disease-weakened body on 
that long journey to come here for this?

19:07.480 --> 19:11.830
The value of the existence of a royal family 
lulled into naïvety by peace is questionable.

19:14.000 --> 19:16.380
Even if, hypothetically, we 
moved this discussion forward,

19:16.380 --> 19:19.180
what does Coyolles intend 
to bring to our empire?

19:19.840 --> 19:24.160
We will promise to give exports of gems and 
metals to your empire the highest priority.

19:25.110 --> 19:27.810
Even if our kingdom makes 
no profit whatsoever.

19:29.220 --> 19:31.120
<i>That won't work, Prince Kyle.</i>

19:31.120 --> 19:33.740
<i>You aren't suited to telling lies.</i>

19:34.650 --> 19:35.890
Don't make me laugh.

19:36.290 --> 19:41.320
If I were in your place, I would be sure to 
attach a period of effectiveness to that offer.

19:42.100 --> 19:44.520
The gems which serve as the 
kingdoms greatest source of funds

19:44.520 --> 19:48.060
cannot continue to be supplied with 
no regard to profit indefinitely.

19:49.150 --> 19:50.490
That's...

19:50.490 --> 19:53.990
It's clear why you've come 
here with such a suggestion.

19:55.520 --> 20:00.090
Coyolles' mineral resources have 
already nearly run dry, haven't they?

20:01.840 --> 20:04.300
<i>Yes, that's right.</i>

20:07.660 --> 20:09.330
It's incomprehensible to me.

20:09.930 --> 20:12.750
Your actions are nothing more 
than the actions of a fool.

20:16.800 --> 20:21.020
My life... isn't likely to last much longer.

20:23.280 --> 20:27.180
A new life is about to be 
born into my royal family!

20:28.000 --> 20:32.440
For the sake of that child's future, 
and for the sake of our people...

20:32.440 --> 20:35.830
I must do whatever I can right now.

20:36.840 --> 20:41.150
From what I've researched, Prince 
Arnold, you care for your people,

20:41.150 --> 20:43.910
and run a government which 
extends a helping hand to them.

20:44.540 --> 20:45.510
If it were you, then—

20:46.510 --> 20:48.370
This isn't worth discussing any further.

20:48.960 --> 20:50.270
Please wait!

20:50.270 --> 20:52.800
Please, Prince Arnold!

20:52.800 --> 20:54.770
Please help Coyolles!

20:56.220 --> 20:59.020
You seem to be mistaken about something.

21:01.560 --> 21:06.660
Rather than joining hands with another 
country, invading and taking control of it...

21:06.960 --> 21:08.910
that suits me much better.

21:17.250 --> 21:18.910
<i>Five years from now...</i>

21:19.290 --> 21:23.470
<i>Prince Arnold will have become emperor 
and will wage war on the world.</i>

21:23.470 --> 21:26.330
<i>Coyolles will fight Galkhein.</i>

21:30.720 --> 21:33.810
<i>And so many lives will be...</i>

21:36.810 --> 21:42.130
<i>But Prince Kyle has confronted Prince 
Arnold and proposed an alliance.</i>

21:42.880 --> 21:46.780
<i>This is a branching point in history 
which could change the future.</i>

21:48.620 --> 21:52.490
Weitzner, I want to protect this kingdom.

21:52.910 --> 21:56.230
To accomplish that, I intend 
to do whatever it takes.

21:57.680 --> 22:01.770
As someone born into this, someone who has 
lived beyond his time, I have duties to perform,

22:02.680 --> 22:04.440
and this is the greatest of them all!

22:08.790 --> 22:12.150
<i>Prince Kyle may be prepared for Coyolles</i>

22:12.150 --> 22:15.520
<i>to become a vassal state to 
Galkhein if it means an alliance.</i>

22:16.010 --> 22:16.950
<i>But...</i>

22:17.520 --> 22:20.020
<i>that would only change who 
is in control of the nation.</i>

22:21.190 --> 22:23.810
<i>Unless a relationship of 
equal standing is created...</i>

22:26.700 --> 22:29.900
<i>But how?</i>
